// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// RDS data providers
//
// For NEW (AWS-onboarded) customers we serve the same screens from the user's own
// AWS RDS MS SQL `core2` database instead of proxying to the RM ONE cloud. Each
// provider here returns the EXACT payload shape the matching rmone-proxy route
// returns, so the frontend renders with the same layout/theme and needs no change.
//
// Every query is tenant-scoped by TenantID (the resolved tenant GUID) and skips
// soft-deleted rows (Deleted = 0 OR NULL). All queries read core2.dbo.* directly.
//
// Schema notes (verified against live core2):
//  - PMM (projects) and Opportunity (opportunities) mirror RM ONE field names.
//  - AspNetUsers has NO single role column — job-title fields (Title/Designation/
//    CurrentJobTitle) carry the readable role; Id is the resource GUID.
//  - ResourceAllocation.ResourceUser = AspNetUsers.Id; .TicketId = project ticket;
//    rows with ResourceUser empty are open demand (unfilled positions).
//  - ResourceWorkItems holds person↔work-item rows (ResourceUser is always set).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
